From 4177b49fadd50fc88d1d5f814a1de8a67adcb5ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 18:03:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Restructure walkaround to 7+4 shots, add windscreen check and
 progress diagram

Drops the two full-side shots (front/back corners already cover both
flanks) and moves Boot into the exterior group since it's opened from
outside; interior gains a Passenger Dashboard angle (glovebox side).

analyze-inspection and check-inspection-photo now explicitly scan the
Front shot's windscreen for cracks/chips/star-fractures as part of the
existing damage check, rather than only looking at bumper/lights/body.

Adds InspectionCarDiagram: a top-down car silhouette with a tick marker
at each exterior angle that fills in as that photo is captured, so a
driver can see at a glance which sides are done without reading labels.
InspectionProgress now shows a live percentage instead of a raw count.
